# M B017 — references/scan-layers.md (rest), skills swagger (EXC-008), template-maintenance
1 CO SEC-007 WF-020~ d=WF | Review disabled certificate validation, accept-all callbacks and plain HTTP for sensitive traffic, accounting for TLS termination topology (SEC-007).
2 XW m=D c=M rel=SEC-015,WF-020 | Upload layer checklist (size limits, storage path safety, file names, content/type assumptions, execution/public-serving risk, authorization) (EXC-015 investigative prompts).
  t: when uploads exist
  s: A scan of an upload endpoint that checks only MIME trust (SEC-015): consistent with WF-020; M's checklist covers size, path and serving risks.
3 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020 | Consider rate limiting where abuse realistically matters (login, reset, expensive anonymous endpoints), not on every endpoint (scan review prompt; no rate-limiting policy in the oracle).
  s: A scan that never considers brute-force protection of the login endpoint: consistent with the oracle; M's checklist asks for it.
4 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020,ARC-029,SEC-010 | Sensitive-data layer checklist (security-relevant logging gaps without demanding logs for every request; response data such as entities returned directly, password hashes, unnecessary PII) (EXC-015 prompts).
  s: A scan that does not inspect API responses for returned password hashes: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist includes it.
5 CO SEC-010 d=WF | Look for logged secrets and payment credentials; review PII; Debug/Trace is not a security boundary (SEC-010).
6 CO SEC-008 SEC-016~ c=M | Match data-at-rest protection to the requirement (one-way password hashing, hashed verification tokens, protected storage, platform encryption, Data Protection for temporary payloads) (SEC-008, SEC-016).
7 CO SEC-013 d=WF | Catches letting privileged operations continue, and security failures silently becoming success, are findings (SEC-013).
8 CO RUN-016 d=WF | Review retries of state-changing operations for duplicate effects (RUN-016).
9 XW m=D c=M rel=WF-020,RUN-015 | Exceptional-conditions layer checklist (unbounded time, memory, rows, file/body size, retries, parallel work) (EXC-015 prompts).
  s: A scan that ignores unbounded request-body size on a public endpoint: consistent with WF-020; M's checklist includes it.
10 CO WF-020 | A theoretical missing limit is not automatically High (WF-020 exploitability-based severity).
11 CO SEC-014 d=WF | Dangerous fallbacks in security-sensitive startup configuration (SEC-014).
12 CO API-007 API-008 d=WF | Unexpected exceptions follow centralized handling and reveal no sensitive information (API-007, API-008).
13 CD WF-020~ WF-009~ m=M k=W c=M | Not claiming the static scan proves security is WF-020/WF-009; remainder: meaningful security-sensitive workflows are identified as candidates for threat modeling or manual review.
  t: when such workflows exist
  x: identify security-sensitive workflows as threat-modeling/manual-review candidates
  s: A scan report silent on multi-step authorization workflows (no claim either way): consistent with WF-020/WF-009; M requires listing them as review candidates.
14 CO WF-020 m=MN | No mechanical pattern/CVSS/OWASP-to-severity mapping (WF-020).
15 XW m=M c=M rel=WF-020,WF-009 | Fixed finding shape: severity tag, file:line and title, OWASP category when applicable, Evidence, Impact, Remediation.
  s: A finding written as a prose paragraph with evidence and severity: consistent with WF-020; M's shape is not followed.
16 CO WF-012 WF-020~ m=MN | Do not invent exploitability the code does not establish (WF-012, WF-020).
17 CO DEP-012 DEP-002~ GOV-013~ m=MN | No second competing API documentation stack without a concrete need (DEP-012 decided Swagger baseline).
18 CO DEP-012 m=DC | The developer-facing requirement is the interactive Swagger UI, not a standalone raw OpenAPI endpoint (DEP-012).
19 CO DEP-012 DEP-003~ m=DC | Swashbuckle.AspNetCore with the version selected through add-dependency (DEP-012, DEP-003).
