37 IA m=MN | template-maintenance is user-invoked only (disable-model-invocation: true): loading/invocation rule of the instruction system.
38 IA m=M | One authoritative owner per policy, pointers elsewhere, decision summaries only in their planning-time owners (instruction ownership).
39 IA m=M | Instruction-ownership invariants (Codex wording).
40 IA m=M | Keep each policy at its trigger; no promotion/demotion for loading convenience (instruction placement).
41 IA m=M | Keep always-loaded files and skill descriptions compact; descriptions start with triggers (instruction loading budget).
42 IA m=M | Hooks fail visibly and point at the owning file instead of restating policy (enforcement-layer design rule).
43 IA m=MN | Product inputs stay inputs and carry no instructions (instruction topology).
44 IA m=M | After maintenance update MAP.md and run the structure checker, fixing every failure (instruction maintenance protocol).
45 IA m=M | For hook/script changes run the changed script with sample input and confirm pass and failure paths (maintenance protocol of the enforcement layer).
46 IA m=M | Maintenance report: files changed, owners added/moved, checker result (instruction maintenance output).
